# Viewer-type isolation (panorama vs model3d)

Reuse shared contracts and chrome when it helps (`TourViewerHandle`, dock
panels, tokens). **Do not** let a fix or polish for one `viewerType` silently
change the other.

## Hard rules

1. **Know the surface.** Before editing hotspot / marker / viewer chrome /
   background styles or markup, identify whether the change is:
   - **Panorama-only** (`viewerType: 'panorama'` — PSV, `src/viewer/`, `.psv-*`,
     most `psv-layer.css`)
   - **Model3d-only** (`viewerType: 'model3d'` — `src/viewer-3d/`,
     `.viewer-3d-*`, `viewer-3d-layer.css`, `.hotspot-3d-*`)
   - **Truly shared** (`src/viewer-shared/`, `hotspot-layer.css`, tokens both
     already consume intentionally)

2. **Scope CSS.** Prefer selectors under the owning container:
   - 3D: `.viewer-3d-container …`, `.hotspot-3d-wrap …`
   - Panorama: `.viewer-container …` / `.psv-*` (not bare global hotspot rules
     unless both types must match **by product decision**)
   - Never “fix” 3D by changing a shared hotspot font/padding token used by
     panorama without checking a panorama tour.

3. **Shared tokens need dual QA.** If you change `--ishare-hotspot-*`, glass
   tokens, or hotspot HTML builders used by both paths, verify **both** a
   panorama tour and a `model3d` tour (or explicitly leave a note that only one
   type was checked and why).

4. **No drive-by viewer restyles.** While fixing one viewer, do not “tidy” the
   other’s background gradient, label size, navbar, or marker chrome unless the
   user asked. Regressions have already landed this way (3D hotspot text scale,
   model clear-color / gradient).

5. **Branch logic, don’t blur it.** Prefer `viewerType` / container class forks
   over one style that almost fits both. Shared components are fine; shared
   **defaults that fight one medium** are not.

## When editing these paths

Treat as high-risk coupling:

- `src/styles/psv-layer.css`, `src/styles/hotspot-layer.css`,
  `src/styles/viewer-3d-layer.css`, `src/styles/components-layer.css` (hotspot /
  glass)
- `src/viewer-shared/buildMarkers.ts`, `src/viewer-shared/**` shared chrome
- `src/viewer/**` (PSV-only), `src/viewer-3d/**`
- `src/styles/globals.css` hotspot / float tokens

## Verify

After visual CSS or marker changes: open one panorama tour and one model3d tour
(or state which type was out of scope). Confirm hotspot label size, pill
padding, and viewer background look unchanged on the type you did not intend to
change.

